---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('activecampaign')!;
const b = appBySlug('aftership-email')!;
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-aftership-email';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-aftership-email');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-aftership-email');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should I compare ActiveCampaign with AfterShip Email?",
    "answer": "Compare ActiveCampaign when your team will own follow-up automation. Evaluate AfterShip Email for checkout flow configuration; demonstrate the required event and operating handoff before choosing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these pages establish a recovery winner?",
    "answer": "No merchant trial or incremental lift is established. The workflows and numeric examples are proposed evaluation tools."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I plan timing and incentives?",
    "answer": "Choose timing from checkout behavior and operating constraints. Recheck purchase, inventory, permission and competing queues at dispatch; no universal timing or discount cap is established."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the numeric example assume?",
    "answer": "A $746 basket at 65% gross margin has $484.90 gross profit at full price. A 13% code removes $96.98 from revenue with unchanged goods cost, before other variable costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Checkout flow configuration: compare event coverage, operator responsibilities and recovery cost with your own Shopify checkout.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:"ActiveCampaign",tool:a.name,reason:"An internal owner maintains email recovery and follow-up branches."},{label:"AfterShip Email",tool:b.name,reason:"Shopify email and SMS flows with value and recent-order filters."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>AfterShip Email</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Evaluation focus</td><td>Cart-triggered email and your team’s follow-up rules</td><td>Shopify email and SMS flows with value and recent-order filters.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Demonstration</td><td>Checkout event, populated cart block and purchase exit</td><td>Checkout flow configuration and purchase suppression</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Current quote for audience, automation and implementation</td><td>Current quote including required channels and service scope</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Compare checkout recovery, not shipment tracking</h2>
<p>AfterShip Email is the marketing product in this comparison. Its abandoned-checkout guide describes configurable delivery timing, minimum checkout value and recent-order filters. Tracking and returns products are separate; using those products does not prove their events are available in an Email recovery flow.</p>
<h2>Rehearse the financing and wholesale exceptions</h2>
<p>For a shopper who opens financing then leaves, inspect the actual checkout event and return URL. Write a reminder that answers payment questions without implying financing approval. For a wholesale basket below minimum order quantity, route the question to a named sales owner instead of automatically discounting an ineligible order. ActiveCampaign is a candidate when your team wants to maintain that follow-up branch; AfterShip Email is a candidate when checkout flow configuration covers the job.</p>
<h2>Inspect filters at the boundary</h2>
<p>Propose carts just below and above your chosen value filter and shoppers with different recent-order counts. Record which flow admits each shopper. Change quantity, make one variant unavailable and complete a purchase while the reminder waits. Inspect the populated checkout destination and remaining queue. These checks determine whether the configured rules match your store; no successful trial is asserted.</p>
<h2>Keep Email and SMS eligibility distinct</h2>
<p>AfterShip documents email and SMS flow blocks, but a checkout email address does not establish SMS eligibility. Its SMS guide says abandonment events from before app installation do not trigger SMS. Check sender setup, destinations and permissions before adding a text branch. Do not replay old events simply to fill that branch.</p>
<h2>Check the ActiveCampaign event before designing branches</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001045964-Abandoned-cart-overview">ActiveCampaign’s cart documentation</a> describes email automation and a cart content block. For Shopify it documents a checkout-stage requirement for data sync. A product-page visitor or anonymous cart is not automatically eligible. Record the integration wait and workflow delay separately, then inspect the actual event payload and destination.</p>
<h2>Retain margin math without implying results</h2>
<p>Illustrative basket: $746 at 65% gross margin has $261.10 goods cost and $484.90 full-price gross profit. A 13% code leaves $649.02 revenue and $387.92 gross profit, a $96.98 reduction. Goods cost is unchanged. Subtract fulfillment, payment, message and return costs before calling the remainder contribution. This does not show an incremental recovery by either product.</p>
<h2>Cut over and measure deliberately</h2>
<p>Inventory Shopify and provider recovery flows, pause competing queues and assign one owner per event and channel. Reconcile opt-outs and purchases before enabling the replacement. Compare deduplicated contribution per eligible shopper over the same window. If a randomized no-message group is feasible, choose allocation and duration from traffic, conversion delay and the effect you need to detect. Keep a rollback owner for broken links or failed purchase exits.</p>
<p>Product scope checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://support.aftership.com/en/email/articles/15440875-how-to-increase-conversions-with-abandoned-checkout-emails">AfterShip Email primary documentation</a>. Select the setup whose demonstrated workflow and staffing model fit your store; no ratings or universal winner are supplied.</p>
<p>Additional sources: <a href="https://support.aftership.com/en/email/articles/15440861-how-to-set-up-a-flow-with-aftership-email">Email and SMS flow blocks</a>; <a href="https://support.aftership.com/en/email/articles/15440894-how-to-enable-abandoned-cart-sms">SMS event limits</a>.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
